# 2026-11-09 cloud seat (Claude Opus 5.5), issue #137, Feshbach amplitude lane. PRE-RUN freeze, prediction first. Integer/rational only, HBP; no JSON.
# Nothing that depends on r was computed for the 3x4 model at r=9 by this lane before these rows. Disclosure: NOTE-R9-WILSON-FESHBACH-AMPLITUDE-20261109.md section 12.
# Compatible with PR #148 rows 01-34 (frozen at b2185df95f44d80a6e526c6c455e5f2e7b22deb8; file blob 4764015294cbb20975d1576c5923768075ef20b7, carried byte-identically to main by af0c70f) and its falsifiers F1-F12. This file adds rows. It changes none of #148's.
# Every result row is conditional on #131's floor accepted_source_assumption=lambda_min_QHQ_whole_GE_94070673/1000000 (H4). The UPPER (Rayleigh-Ritz) counts are the only floor-free outputs.
# Row tags: DERIVED (proved in the NOTE), CONJECTURE (a frozen prediction, falsifiable by the r=9 run), OPEN (not known before the run), REQUIRED (a rule the run and the release must obey).
# A basis= field records pre-freeze evidence: MEASURED only for r-independent combinatorics or excluded r>9 smoke; REPORTED for inputs from other lanes. No basis field ever records an r=9 value of the 3x4 model from this lane.
# Verdict words: PASS (every named check passes), REFUSE (a named check fails: no result is reported), HOLD (every check passes but isolation fails or a_lo<=0: #137 stays OPEN), FALSIFIED (a frozen row is contradicted by the run).
# Verdicts are set at the verdict depth only (row 131: depth 5 in the r=9 run). Shallower depths are ladder entries: their check outcomes are reported, and they never stop the run or set a verdict.
# A FALSIFIED CONJECTURE row affects that prediction only. It does not change any theorem.
# A planted fault is refused when its run does not end in PASS and its named check is executed and reported FAIL. Only PF07, PF14 and the skip variant of PF08, whose planted fault is the absence of the named check, are refused by that check being reported missing. A planted fault that ends in PASS falsifies this package. A run-integrity FAIL takes effect at the end of the program step in which it occurs, after every check of that step has printed its CHECK row (no abort before the rows are printed), and a fault run always reaches the step that runs its named check (row 131). The one exception is FREEZE_PIN (rows 030, 113): it is a program step of its own and runs first in the engine and in the driver, and its FAIL, once its own CHECK row is printed, stops the program at once, before any other step or any arithmetic, in every run, fault runs included; neither the step-end clause nor the fault-run clause ever delays it, and PF17 is refused by that FAIL.
# The run's gamma0 (check FLOOR_PIN, row 041) is exactly 94070673/1000000 at r=9 and exactly 94070673/1000000+3(r-9) (row 010, #131's floor plus the Weyl step) at excluded r>9, which covers the smoke, X6, X7 and the r=12 CI runs. Every rule that names gamma0 uses the run's gamma0.
# Output labels: BOUND (the one reportable bound, row 063, from the reported route at the verdict depth only), LADDER (a ladder-depth row), INFORMATIVE (a row of the non-reported route, and the Lemma-7-only a_lo of row 062). LADDER and INFORMATIVE values are measurements for the CONJECTURE table, never bounds.
# A CONJECTURE row whose measured quantity is NOT_EVALUATED or missing is FALSIFIED, except where the row itself predicts NOT_EVALUATED (row 088's depth-2 clause and row 133). Only one sub-row of a run-integrity check may be NOT_EVALUATED: A_a_lo_le_raw of SQ_BOUNDS, where the F_GAP gate withheld its input (rows 060, 131). It is reported, not counted as a FAIL, and SQ_BOUNDS passes iff every evaluated sub-row passes and at least one sub-row is evaluated.
# GPT-6's design audit of #137 (issue #137 comment 6747959074, 2026-11-09, posted before any frozen r=9 measurement) is carried by the REQUIRED rows 146-151 (sec=audit), one per audit item, each mapped to the rows that answer it. Its two exact counterexamples are the negative-control receipts 141-142 (sec=negctl). The floor source is pinned by FLOOR_PIN (rows 041, 136); the sector-to-whole lift is not audited by this package.
